  <example number="3.33">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Model: $$5 - (-3).$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Interpret the expression.</cell>
            <cell>$$5 - (-3)$$ means $$5$$ take away $$-3$$ .</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Model the first number. Start with 5 positives.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Take away the second number, so take away 3 negatives.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>But there are no negatives to take away.Add neutral pairs until you have 3 negatives.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Then take away 3 negatives.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Count the number of counters that are left.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell>The difference of $$5$$ and $$-3$$ is $$8$$ . $$5 - (-3) = 8$$</cell>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
