  <heading level="2">Translate Word Phrases to Algebraic Expressions</heading>
  <paragraph>When we first introduced the operation symbols, we saw that the expression $$a - b$$ may be read in several ways as shown below.</paragraph>
  <figure number="3.18">
    <image alt="This table has six rows. The first row has a - b. The second row states a minus b. The third row states the difference of a and b. The fourth row states subtract b from a. The fifth row states b subtracted from a. The sixth row states b less than a."/>
  </figure>
  <paragraph>Be careful to get $$a$$ and $$b$$ in the right order!</paragraph>
  <example number="3.43">
